# Qlix — core schema

Relational model for identity (Layer 3), audit (Layer 5), orgs, and API access. Adjust names to Prisma conventions (`camelCase` fields, `@id`, `DateTime`, etc.) but preserve semantics.

## `users`

- `id`, `email`, `name`, `avatar_url`, `created_at`, `updated_at`

## `organizations`

- `id`, `name`, `slug`, `plan` (`free` | `pro` | `enterprise`), `created_at`

## `org_members`

- `id`, `org_id`, `user_id`, `role` (`owner` | `admin` | `member`), `joined_at`

## `agents`

- `id`, `name`, `did`, `owner_type` (`user` | `org`), `owner_id`
- `status` (`active` | `idle` | `suspended`), `created_at`, `last_active_at`

## `credentials`

- `id`, `agent_id`, `vc_type`, `issuer_did`, `issued_at`, `expires_at`, `revoked_at`, `payload_json`

## `audit_events`

- `id`, `agent_id`, `org_id` (nullable for individual context), `action_type`
- `description`, `result` (`success` | `blocked` | `flagged`)
- `actor_type` (`agent` | `admin` | `system`), `actor_id`
- `metadata_json`, `created_at`

## `api_keys`

- `id`, `owner_type` (`user` | `org`), `owner_id`
- `key_hash`, `label`, `last_used_at`, `created_at`, `revoked_at`

## Notes

- Store **hashes** for API keys at rest; never log raw keys.
- `audit_events.org_id` aligns org-wide views and CSV export eligibility with org plans.
- Index hot paths: `audit_events(created_at)`, `audit_events(agent_id, created_at)`, `agents(owner_type, owner_id)`.
